# STOP AT `npm i`, NOT SOMEWHERE IN THE SUITE.
#
# `engines` in package.json is ADVISORY by default: npm prints a warning nobody reads and installs
# anyway. The README's promise is `npm i && npm test` → green, so on an unsupported Node the first
# thing a stranger sees is not "you need Node 20", it is a stack trace from whichever API is missing
# — and the obvious conclusion is that the repo is broken.
#
# With this, npm refuses at install and names the version it needs. `setup.sh` already checked; the
# path the README actually advertises did not.
engine-strict=true
